  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Angle back, angle forward – 7 v 7",
  "description": "Seven against seven with goalkeepers on a pitch of about 55 × 40 metres. Only passes along the ground are allowed, and each player has at most three touches. A lofted pass gives the ball to the opponents.\n\nScoring: a goal is worth one point. If the attack included a diagonal pass backwards followed straight away by a diagonal pass forwards, the goal is worth two – the coach calls it out when it happens. The players off the ball keep moving so the ball carrier always has an angle back and an angle forward.\n\nVariation: play with offside if the team does in matches, or drop to two touches when it flows. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Stand at an angle, never straight behind or straight in front of an opponent – the passing lane is closed there."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Play diagonally back to buy time, and look straight away for the diagonal forward."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Receive on the right foot with an open body, so the next pass goes on one or two touches."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Pass firmly along the ground, to the foot furthest from the opponent."
    }
  ],
